## Roadmap item and goal

PR B / ARK3 — semantic roadmap normalization after the process bootstrap from PR #1.

Goal: convert the existing milestone-level plan into an executable dependency-aware backlog without starting any Bloodborne/shadPS4 correctness, instrumentation, or performance implementation work.

## What changed

- preserved the project goal, milestone sequence, upstream-first direction, correctness-before-specialization constraint, and exit intent from the original roadmap;
- replaced milestone-only bullets with **34 bounded roadmap items** using stable `BB-*` IDs;
- added explicit status, priority, execution class, dependencies, question, next experiment / expected information gain, acceptance/artifact destination, and scope for each item;
- kept `BB-BL1`, `BB-BL2`, and `BB-BL3` as the only ready-now independent items;
- added `BB-ENV1`, a named **CLOUD RESEARCH feasibility dependency** that must resolve the concrete target-execution route/handoff before any `GATED` run may start;
- made every `GATED` roadmap item directly depend on `BB-ENV1`, so `GATED` no longer means an unresolvable generic “needs target machine” state;
- removed the global correctness rollup (`BB-COR6`) from the independent resource/sync/graphics seam paths: `BB-FIX1/3/5` now depend only on their corresponding reproduced symptom class;
- added `BB-COR7`, an explicit **correctness-sufficient-for-profiling gate**; optimization-ranking datasets and post-correctness corpora stay blocked until key correctness paths are fixed/verified, closed by negative evidence, or explicitly bounded as non-distorting;
- explicitly allow pre-`BB-COR7` **reproducibility baseline and bounded diagnostic measurements** required by correctness/instrumentation (`BB-BL6`, `BB-INS4`), avoiding a policy-level dependency cycle while keeping `BB-SHD2`, `BB-RES2`, and `BB-PERF2` post-gate;
- split performance work so `BB-PERF1` is a cloud-only non-overlapping accounting model, `BB-PERF2` is the separate `GATED` repeated target dataset collection, and `BB-PERF3` ranks the measured bottlenecks offline;
- added explicit stale-evidence handling: a correctness fix that changes source/target/config baseline must reopen/reconcile affected baseline, instrumentation, corpus, and performance captures rather than compare stale datasets;
- kept unknown future correctness/performance classes dynamic: confirmed distinct classes and measured optimization candidates get new bounded IDs when evidence exists rather than being invented during normalization;
- kept explicit provenance requirements for emulator source, Bloodborne target, host environment, scenario, and capture/tool version;
- removed the temporary bootstrap-transition guard from `docs/agent-policy.local.md` now that the roadmap is executable;
- reconciled generated `AGENTS.md` and `.agentic-repo.lock.json` for that local-policy change.

## Evidence and reasoning

### Established

- PR #1 is merged into `main`, so this PR starts from the self-contained agent contract rather than a stacked bootstrap branch.
- Before this change the roadmap preserved useful product intent but had no stable item IDs, explicit dependency graph, execution gating, or per-item acceptance/artifact contracts.
- Review exposed five execution-model defects across the normalization iterations: no named target-feasibility gate, mixed cloud/target work in `BB-PERF1`, unnecessary global fan-in through `BB-COR6`, no correctness gate before optimization profiling/specialization, and an over-broad gate sentence that accidentally blocked the baseline/diagnostic measurements needed to reach `BB-COR7`. The current graph/contract addresses each explicitly.
- The normalized graph contains **34 unique items and 77 dependency edges**. Every dependency resolves to an existing item and the graph is acyclic.
- Exactly three items have zero roadmap dependencies: `BB-BL1`, `BB-BL2`, and `BB-BL3`, matching the `Ready now` section.
- Every item classified `GATED` names `BB-ENV1` directly as a dependency.
- Unknown root causes remain investigations. Title-visible VRAM, synchronization, or rendering symptoms do not directly authorize a patch; per-class seam investigations can proceed independently once their own reproduction evidence exists.

### Still hypotheses / unknowns

- The exact shadPS4 upstream repository/commit and source-integration model are deliberately left to `BB-BL1`.
- The Bloodborne build/content identity, target scenarios, host baseline, target-execution feasibility, currently reproducible correctness symptoms, and any performance numbers remain unknown.
- No claim is made that the listed historical symptom classes still reproduce on the future pinned baseline.
- Later captures may show that multiple symptom classes share one root cause or that an originally listed class is stale; the roadmap explicitly preserves that possibility.

## Validation

- GitHub compare: branch is **4 commits ahead** of current `main` and still changes only four files: `ROADMAP.md`, `docs/agent-policy.local.md`, generated `AGENTS.md`, and `.agentic-repo.lock.json`.
- Semantic roadmap validation after review fixes: **34 unique IDs**, **77 resolved dependency edges**, **0 dependency cycles**, only `BB-BL1..3` dependency-free, and **0 `GATED` items without direct `BB-ENV1` dependency**.
- The latest P1 fix changes only the execution-contract wording relative to the previously reviewed head: pre-gate baseline/diagnostic measurements are allowed, while optimization-ranking datasets and post-correctness corpora remain explicitly gated by `BB-COR7`.
- Generated-contract reconciliation from the first commit remains unchanged: removing only the bootstrap-transition local fragment produces the committed `AGENTS.md`; its SHA-256 matches the updated lock entry. Other generated inputs/config/profiles are unchanged.
- Markdown/link inspection: the regenerated `AGENTS.md` keeps the previously valid relative links; the normalized roadmap introduces no relative Markdown links requiring new targets.
- The full `agentic-repo check` CLI was not executed in this connector-only environment; no claim is made otherwise.

## Target/environment validation

Not applicable. Bloodborne and shadPS4 were not executed. This PR contains planning/process state only and establishes no target-runtime facts.

## Roadmap / durable knowledge

- [x] milestone intent preserved;
- [x] executable stable IDs/dependencies added;
- [x] evidence vs hypothesis boundary explicit;
- [x] named target-execution feasibility gate added;
- [x] cloud preparation separated from target execution;
- [x] independent correctness seams no longer blocked by unrelated symptom classes;
- [x] correctness-sufficient-for-profiling gate added without blocking prerequisite baseline/diagnostic measurements;
- [x] stale baseline/corpus/performance recapture rule explicit;
- [x] target provenance required before runtime claims;
- [x] negative-result/supersession behavior preserved;
- [x] target-specific artifacts have durable destinations under `docs/` rather than chat-only instructions.

### Process contract

- [x] One primary bounded outcome: normalize the roadmap.
- [x] No correctness/instrumentation implementation item is started in this PR.
- [x] After merge, normal one-roadmap-item-per-PR development may begin with `BB-BL1`, `BB-BL2`, or `BB-BL3`.

## Deliberately out of scope

- pinning the actual shadPS4 baseline (`BB-BL1`);
- defining actual Bloodborne target identity values (`BB-BL2`);
- resolving target execution feasibility (`BB-ENV1`);
- collecting host/runtime data;
- selecting gameplay scenarios;
- reproducing any correctness symptom;
- adding shadPS4 source instrumentation/fixes;
- collecting shader/resource corpora or performance measurements;
- deciding that a Bloodborne-specific runtime is beneficial.
